comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-06T20:10:05.198Z","harness:claude-code","Fix: in TOON, an omission receipt equal to the complete shape (has_omissions false, count 0, no groups) renders as the single line omission_receipt: complete; receipts that report omissions are unchanged and JSON/SDK/MCP keep the typed receipt. For an explicit get --fields selection (command get with a non-empty fields option) the host passes preserveEmptyItemCollections to formatBuiltInOutput, which restores every empty array or object the projection kept in item, in order, after the sparse policy drops them (unrequested empty groups are never in the projection, so they stay absent). Measured: pm get <id> --fields id,title,comments on a fresh tracker went from 162 B (receipt 96 B, 59%) to 105 B (receipt 27 B, 26%) and now shows comments: []. The unit spec compares the four-line receipt (share above a third) with the new rendering (below a third)."
